      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Taft’s early economy exploded when Union Oil Company of California and other firms built camps and derricks along the Sunset siding in the 1910s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
